# Directories whose name ends in ";C" are not real: they are what Git Bash
# leaves behind when a docker bind mount is written without MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1.
# It rewrites "-v /f/path:/container" into "F:\path;C:\Program Files\Git\container",
# docker takes the whole string as one source path, and creates a directory
# literally called "<path>;C". Three of them were reported as issue #78.
#
# Prefix every docker command that bind-mounts a path from Git Bash with
# MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1. This line only stops the debris being committed; it
# cannot stop it being created.
*;C
*;C/
